@startuml
title SwiftLint analysis in pre-commit and CI
start
:Pre-commit or CI requests project-wide analysis
(including deletion-only commits);
:Copy canonical Xcode dependency pins
to ignored Package.resolved;
:Resolve the package graph for the selected Xcode;
:Clean and build Swift package tests
and iOS app with hosted tests;
note right
  Dedicated build/SwiftLintAnalyze outputs.
  Reuse dependency downloads, never old compiler logs.
  No app signing or test execution required.
end note
if (Builds succeed and Xcode pins unchanged?) then (yes)
  :Combine iOS then package build logs;
  :Unescape Xcode's macro-plugin hash separators;
  :Run unused_import and unused_declaration with
  swiftlint analyze --strict --compiler-log-path;
  if (Findings or compiler/analyzer diagnostics?) then (yes)
    :Fail hook / CI;
  elseif (Analyzed file count matches all sources/tests?) then (yes)
    :Pass hook / CI;
  else (no)
    :Fail: incomplete file count;
  endif
else (no)
  :Fail with build log;
endif
stop
@enduml
